license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  DSFB-Chemical-Engineering is a deterministic, read-only residual-interpretation
  layer for chemical process monitoring. It ingests the residuals, scores,
  distances, reconstruction errors, contribution traces, and detector
  disagreements emitted by established chemometrics detectors (PCA, PLS, DPCA,
  KPCA, ICA, EWMA, CUSUM, contribution plots, autoencoders, …) and applies
  Drift–Slew Fusion Bootstrap — drift, slew, admissibility envelopes, detector
  consensus, and a chemical heuristics bank — to produce auditable,
  human-readable structural episodes and a replayable, byte-exact evidence case
  file. It does not replace any estimator, controller, historian, or alarm
  system; it structures the diagnostic exhaust those systems already produce.
